The XPM was converted from the supplied Project9 logo. The xlogin
resources use the names in OpenBSD Xenodm's config/Xresources.in.
These source assets are ready for the display manager port. They do
not start a greeter.

The kernel still needs an authenticated local display handoff for
non-root sessions. The upstream doas port also needs distinct real
and effective credentials and secure set-user-ID execution.
